README.OSK -- what was changed to build REBUILT/screen_nocio herescandir.c: `filecnt' is now set to 0.  The original declares it`register int filecnt;' and never initialises it, then stores each fileit accepts at dirlist[filecnt++] -- so the first store went wherever theregister happened to point.  Under os9exec that was a bus error at thefirst file accepted from $HOME/.SCREENS (measured 2026-09-22, in both thisbuild and the archive's own); on the machine it was written on theregister evidently held something harmless.  One line; nothing else ischanged.  CMDS/screen is the archive's own cio build and still has it.